  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/johannes-schmieder/fevc/zipball/v0.6.0",
  "body": "fevc 0.6.0 adds repeat-measurement standard errors by default and supports Stata 15 or later.\n\n- Reports one normal or q=1 interval for each supported component; use `inference(none)` for point estimates only.\n- Replaces the experimental variance-model options from 0.5.2 with the repeat-measurement method. See the inference guide for supported routes, assumptions and limitations.\n- Fixes inference dispatch for explicit generic/diagonal requests on Windows and compatibility with older Stata runtime interfaces and diagnostic tables.\n- Includes five native binaries built from common source `2082f20974d6437814905c351f13509ff934d04e`, qualified on macOS, Linux and Windows. Stata 15.1 full, installed-native and actual-default tests pass on Mac under Rosetta.\n\nThe release includes the installation ZIP, corresponding source, manifest and checksums. Restart Stata after upgrading a loaded native plugin. Windows qualification covers Stata 19 with one/two workers; native Intel hardware and Stata 16/17 execution are not claimed.\n\n[Installation](https://github.com/johannes-schmieder/fevc/blob/v0.6.0/INSTALLATION.md) \u00b7 [Inference guide](https://github.com/johannes-schmieder/fevc/blob/v0.6.0/fevc/docs/INFERENCE.md)\n"
